    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #60 Update: Fee-Drag Mitigation & Whipsaw Filtering\nOut-of-sample testing in Cycle #60 demonstrated strong directional alpha via DeepSeek V4.1 Flash (53.8% win rate, positive gross P&L of \u20b919.92), but statutory fee drag (\u20b947.79) and mid-morning stop whipsaws (particularly the Oct 22 cluster in `TATASTEEL`, `ITC`, and `AXISBANK`) resulted in a net loss of \u20b9-27.87. To overcome structural transaction costs on our micro-capital base, we are widening `min_sl_pct` from 0.55% to 0.65% to absorb 5-minute market microstructure noise, while expanding `min_target_pct` from 1.0% to 1.35% to ensure winning trades generate sufficient gross profit to comfortably cover brokerage and STT. Simultaneously, we are tightening entry selectivity by increasing `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to 2.65x to filter out low-conviction mid-day drifts, and lowering `breakeven_trigger_r` to 0.95R to aggressively protect capital against EOD decay."
